SCOPE — what this licence does and does not cover

The MIT licence above applies to the SOURCE CODE in this repository: the Python
modules, tests, configuration, Dockerfiles and documentation.

It does NOT apply to:

1. PODCAST CONTENT.
   `data/index/chunks.json` contains machine-generated transcript excerpts from
   published podcast episodes. Those words belong to the speakers who said them,
   including interview guests, and are included here solely so the retrieval
   demo can function. They are not licensed for reuse, redistribution or
   republication. The source audio is not distributed with this repository.

2. THIRD-PARTY MODEL WEIGHTS.
   `models/minilm-onnx/` contains an ONNX export of `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`,
   distributed under the Apache License 2.0 by its original authors. See
   `models/minilm-onnx/SOURCE.md` for provenance.

If you want to reuse the code, take it — that is what the MIT licence is for.
If you want to quote the transcripts, ask the speakers.
